 `priority` is optional (`normal`). Answers 201 with the new ticket, whose status is `open`. The requester is notified
 that the ticket was received.
 
+### Import tickets: `POST /tickets/import`
+
+```json
+{ "tickets": [ { "title": "VPN drops every hour", "requester": "maria@example.com" }, { "title": "...", "requester": "..." } ] }
+```
+
+Each item is what `POST /tickets` takes; at most 5000. The tickets are created in the given order, all of them or none:
+if any item is invalid the answer is 400 and nothing is created, and the message names the first invalid item by its
+index in the array (`tickets[0]` is the first). Answers 201 with `{ "created": 3, "ids": ["T-0043", "T-0044", "T-0045"] }`.
+Each ticket is recorded in the audit log and its requester notified, as when it is created on its own. This endpoint
+accepts bodies up to 8 MiB whatever `MAX_BODY_BYTES` is.
+
 ### List tickets: `GET /tickets`
 
 | Parameter | Meaning |
